+### Time Format Compound
+
+Use `compound: true` to break a duration into multiple parts, largest unit first. Zero parts are skipped, the largest unit is days and the smallest is seconds (leftover milliseconds are dropped, so values under one second give `"0s"`). It takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(7200000, { compound: true })       // "2h"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+ms(500, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
